steps.detail:
In input_evdev.c, behaviour unchanged:
- Add ABS_MT_TOUCH_MAJOR and ABS_MT_SLOT absinfo to the open-time axis log (1283-1286).
- Per session, log the median and maximum TOUCH_MAJOR of single fingertip contacts, for T_palm.
- Add the opt-in grimoire/touch-trace file (format 1: F frames with kernel ms, slot, id, logical x and y, major and tool; P pen-state lines with no coordinates; E outcome lines). Written only while input is grabbed, never at the PIN, capped at 4 MB, never exported.
- The docs/KINDLE.md owner script adds:
  - one-finger Z, N, S, circle, alpha and triangle, 10 each;
  - one-finger swipes, 10 each way;
  - 10 one-finger V shapes;
  - 5 minutes of writing with the palm resting;
  - 2 minutes holding the Kindle and reading.

touchgest stamps IN_TOUCH_DOWN/MOVE/UP with:
- k_ms: the SYN_REPORT kernel time through pensync_ms;
- value bit 0, TOUCH_F_BROAD: TOUCH_MAJOR above T_palm at any frame of this contact's session (log-only until the trace is read);
- value bit 1, TOUCH_F_CANCEL: the off-screen cancel (x and y stay -10000).
In record mode, a single-finger landing it suppresses for the pen window is reported as a pen rejection (IN_GESTURE with a negative value), as the plan does for multi-finger tries.

steps.tests:
test_touchgest:
- k_ms survives a simulated 1.2 s read stall with real spacing;
- the BROAD flag sets at T_palm+1, not at T_palm;
- the CANCEL flag on second-contact, palm and pen-arrival cancels, never on a real lift;
- the record-mode pen rejection for one finger.
All pinch scenarios stay green.

s_fit_1:
- rotate 1: editor.zoom is 1.00 and the view equals zoom_min;
- swipe 2 down mid-screen opens Pages;
- pinch in, then pan mid-screen; next page returns to the whole page; Fit page returns to it;
- the Display toggle gives the width fit, and the setting persists across a restart;
- the landscape-fit key toggles it; upright toggling only toasts;
- the hint shows once.
y_all_screens sideways with the new Display row under CHECK_FIT in EN/ES and both styles. Every existing scenario stays green, with the header line where needed.

test_gesturemap:
- shape lines with the overlays;
- '=nothing' leaves shapes alone;
- the carried-line limits;
- an unreadable file is never written;
- Reset deletes the file.
test_actions: every SHAPE-capable action has labels, and hold-eraser is not SHAPE.
